WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.930
Why register, which structure, and how to get ready safely.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:09.980
This is the video for module one of Business Registration and Compliance in Nigeria.

3
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:17.440
Registration turns your hustle into something the law, banks and big customers can see and trust.

4
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:32.740
In Nigeria, the Corporate Affairs Commission, the CAC, registers businesses under the Companies and Allied Matters Act 2020, called CAMA 2020. Once your name is registered, nobody else can register it.

5
00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:38.880
Banks ask for CAC documents before opening an account in a business name.

6
00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:46.590
Supermarkets, schools, hotels and government agencies usually ask for them before they buy from you.

7
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.110
Many grants, loans and trainings ask for registration as proof you are serious.

8
00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:01.530
And NAFDAC asks for CAC registration before it registers a food, drink or cosmetic product.

9
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:11.210
For example, Halima in Kaduna makes groundnut oil and kuli-kuli, sells to two supermarkets and on WhatsApp, and wants a bank loan.

10
00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:17.870
CAC: yes. The supermarkets pay a business account, and the bank lends to a business.

11
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:31.630
Tax: yes. She confirms her Tax ID and keeps records so she can file, even if the tax due is small. Note that the old FIRS is now the Nigeria Revenue Service, NRS.

12
00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:39.430
NAFDAC: yes. Packaged food sold to the public needs NAFDAC registration for each product.

13
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.240
SON: no. Her products are food, which NAFDAC regulates.

14
00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:54.130
Knowing the order stops her paying for things in the wrong sequence. A tailor or hairdresser needs CAC and tax, but not NAFDAC.

15
00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:08.070
A business name is the trading name of a person or partnership. It is simple and usually cheapest. But the law sees you and the business as one. If the business owes money, you personally owe it.

16
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:19.180
A private limited company is a separate legal person. If it fails, shareholders generally lose only what they put in, not their homes or savings.

17
00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:29.190
Under CAMA 2020, one person can form a company, and the minimum issued share capital is 100,000 naira, at the time of writing.

18
00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:40.190
For example, three women in Lagos. Bisi sells ankara bags from home. She is one person with low risk, so a business name is enough for now.

19
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:51.490
Chioma and her sister will sign catering contracts, with a risk of a large claim if food goes wrong. A limited company protects their personal property.

20
00:02:52.740 --> 00:03:00.060
Funmi wants an investor for her drinks factory. An investor can only buy shares in a company, not a business name.

21
00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:09.110
Ask yourself: if this business failed tomorrow, could I pay its debts without losing my home? If not, think seriously about a company.

22
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:19.900
Most delays happen before the form is submitted. So prepare three distinctive names, and avoid words like Federal, National or Bank without approval.

23
00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:29.010
Have your NIN, and use your name exactly as on your NIN record. Add a clear photo, a dark-pen signature and real addresses.

24
00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.590
Use your own email and phone, and have a way to pay. Then you can finish in one sitting.

25
00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:45.160
Fees change, so always use the current fee shown on the CAC portal when you pay, not a figure from a blog. Pay only through the official portal.

26
00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:54.000
If you use an agent, check their accreditation on the CAC website, and make sure the business is registered in your name, with your email.

27
00:03:55.250 --> 00:04:10.270
Be careful of people promising same day CAC for cash to a personal account. The CAC will never need your bank PIN or OTP. And never send your NIN, photo or signature in an open WhatsApp group.

28
00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:29.660
To remember. The CAC registers businesses under CAMA 2020. With a business name, you are personally liable. A company is a separate person with limited liability. Prepare names and documents first. And never share your bank PIN or OTP.

29
00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:38.740
Now draw your compliance map, write your structure decision, and build your registration kit with three searched names and a budget.

30
00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.030
Continue with the lessons below.
